    {
      "id": "P1",
      "text": "UPPER ENDOSCOPY (EGD) REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 4, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Isaac Brandvold, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Vomiting and solid-food intolerance after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass in 2025."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "Anatomy: small gastric pouch with a gastrojejunal anastomosis to a Roux limb."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "Procedure: The gastroscope was advanced through a normal esophagus into the gastric pouch."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "At the gastrojejunal anastomosis there was a tight stricture with a lumen of about 4 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "The gastroscope could not be passed through the stricture."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "A guidewire was passed through the stricture under direct vision into the Roux limb."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "A wire-guided balloon was positioned across the stricture and inflated to 6, 7 and 8 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "After dilation the gastroscope still could not traverse the anastomosis."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "The Roux limb was therefore not examined endoscopically."
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "text": "1. Gastrojejunal anastomotic stricture, balloon-dilated to 8 mm over a guidewire."
    },
    {
      "id": "P14",
      "text": "2. The gastroscope reached the anastomosis only; only the guidewire entered the Roux limb."
    },
    {
      "id": "P15",
      "text": "Plan: Repeat balloon dilation in 3 weeks."
    }
  ],
